{"name":"Santana Soul","hex":"#714636","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"soul","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The spirit or essence of a person usually thought to consist of one's thoughts and personality, often believed to live on after the person's death.","The spirit or essence of anything."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Characteristic of or pertaining to African American culture."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soul"}],"entries":[{"title":"Santana (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Santana is an American rock band formed in San Francisco, California in 1966 by Mexican-American guitarist Carlos Santana. The band has had various recording and performing line-ups in its history, with Santana being the only consistent member. After signing with Columbia Records, the band's appearance at the Woodstock Festival in 1969 increased their profile and they went on to record the critically acclaimed and commercially successful albums Santana (1969), Abraxas (1970) and Santana III (1971). These were recorded by the group's \"classic\" line-up, comprising organist and lead vocalist Gregg Rolie, percussionists José \"Chepito\" Areas and Michael Carabello, drummer Michael Shrieve and bassist David Brown. Hit songs of this period include \"Evil Ways\" (1970), \"Black Magic Woman\" (1970), \"Oye Como Va\" (1971) and the instrumental \"Samba Pa Ti\" (1970)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Santana_%281971%29.png/330px-Santana_%281971%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santana_(band)"},{"title":"Soul","blocks":[{"text":"In religion and philosophy, the soul is the immaterial aspect or essence of a living being. It is typically believed to be immortal and to exist apart from the material world. Anthropologists and psychologists have found that most humans believe in the existence of a soul or spirit, and that they have cross-culturally distinguished between the soul and the material body."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Schiavonetti_Soul_leaving_body_1808.jpg/330px-Schiavonetti_Soul_leaving_body_1808.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soul"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Woodstock_redmond_stage.JPG/500px-Woodstock_redmond_stage.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Woodstock_redmond_stage.JPG/500px-Woodstock_redmond_stage.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Santana rose to prominence following their appearance at Woodstock","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWoodstock_redmond_stage.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Santana_1973_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Santana_1973_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Santana_1973_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Santana_1973_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Carlos Santana in 1973","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASantana_1973_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Santana_Acer_Arena_%285558204467%29.jpg/500px-Santana_Acer_Arena_%285558204467%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Santana_Acer_Arena_%285558204467%29.jpg/1280px-Santana_Acer_Arena_%285558204467%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Santana_Acer_Arena_%285558204467%29.jpg/500px-Santana_Acer_Arena_%2